From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:46:11 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: show the backlog and fix the font metrics in the sg-pc
 profile

TYN-only (profile data plus two small SGHD conditions).

Backlog. The STEINS;GATE (Steam) scripts open the backlog through the Chaos;Child style MesRev routine
(Unk0110 modes 0..5 in the SGHD disassembler, a KeyOnJump poll of PADcustom[12] in the system loop), and
InstMesRev only showed and hid the BacklogMenu for MO6TW and MO6TWPC, so nothing was drawn. Add SGHD to
both. The scripts poll the Backlog pad button, not the F2 keyboard key the flick/wheel synthesizes, so
UpdatePADInput also raises PADcustom[12] for SGHD when the wheel scrolls down or a flick goes down. The
profile now uses the measured BACKLOG.DDS sheet: panel with the BACKLOG header (x 0..1790), scrollbar track
(x 1790..1823), thumb (1940,58,12x103), voice icon (1974,6,59x54); the sheet has no highlight or controls
strip, which use a transparent patch. The backlog shows the chapter title, names, text and voice icons.

Font. The profile inherited the Chaos;Child advance table, which describes another typeface: round Latin
letters ("o", "O", "?") were cut off at the right edge of their cell because SingleSheetFont crops a glyph
quad to its advance width. font-widths.lua is generated from the font atlas by
tools/impacto/sghd/gen_widths.py (ink right edge + 3 for the proportional Latin glyphs, ids 1..226; space 16;
48 for everything else) and font.lua uses it with a 48px em.

Charset. Digits and Latin letters (ids 1..62 and the second copy of the set at 128..189, which the script
text uses) are flagged Alphabet so the line breaker no longer splits words ("asph|alt") and only breaks at
spaces and punctuation.

Checked on MuMu (Android 15): the first scenes render with correct glyph shapes and spacing, flick down
opens the backlog with the prologue lines, names, voice icons and scrollbar thumb, and the text wraps at word
boundaries.

diff --git a/profiles/sg-pc/charset.lua b/profiles/sg-pc/charset.lua
index f0d1c2adea059ba415ca3739d6db9f3a6ecf6c8b..5b9524909a573f66d541f0c4a0b606dc9713a716 100644
--- a/profiles/sg-pc/charset.lua
+++ b/profiles/sg-pc/charset.lua
@@ -9,6 +9,14 @@ for i = 0, #spaces do
     root.Charset.Flags[spaces[i]] = root.Charset.Flags[spaces[i]] | CharacterTypeFlags.Space;
 end
 
+-- Digits and Latin letters, in both copies of the Latin set in the font atlas (ids 1..62 in rows 0-1 and the same
+-- glyphs 127 ids later, 128..189, which the script text uses). Flagging them as Alphabet keeps the line breaker from
+-- splitting a word in the middle (it may only break at a non-Alphabet glyph, i.e. a space or punctuation).
+for i = 1, 62 do
+    root.Charset.Flags[i] = root.Charset.Flags[i] | CharacterTypeFlags.Alphabet;
+    root.Charset.Flags[i + 127] = root.Charset.Flags[i + 127] | CharacterTypeFlags.Alphabet;
+end
+
